---
const stages = [
  [
    'Find records',
    'Search and filters narrow the audit list and lead to a detailed workspace.',
  ],
  [
    'Review context',
    'Audit details, lifecycle, milestones, and progress provide a shared view of the work.',
  ],
  [
    'Connect documents & analysis',
    'Attachments, SharePoint folder sync, analytical context, and document-informed assistance support investigation.',
  ],
  [
    'Save & trace changes',
    'Permitted users save deliberate updates; conflict handling and history preserve context around changes.',
  ],
];
---

<figure
  class="case-study-workflow architecture-flow"
  aria-label="Conceptual record workflow"
>
  <ol>
    {stages.map(([title, description], index) => (
      <li>
        <span class="flow-number" aria-hidden="true">
          {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
        </span>
        <div>
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p>{description}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <p class="flow-foundation">
    Across the workflow: Microsoft Entra ID, application roles, and server-side
    authorization.
  </p>
  <figcaption>
    Conceptual application workflow showing implemented capabilities. Not a
    screenshot of the internal application.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
